---
/**
 * P6 Universities: /partner-with-us/universities/ (T3, implements doc 04 matrix 4.5).
 * C1 to C14 in order, as the numbered table in doc 06 P6, without C3 (Cost of Waiting) and C4 (Imagine), which the audience pages leave to Home since WP47.
 * WP30c (owner direction 2026-10-14, "less is more"): every CMF band stays, each states its point once. Gone: the In Short summary, the fit check, the
 * standard-inclusions list, the restated scorecard paragraph and the fifth next step.
 * WP36 (cycle-13 reviews): the three pains are statements; the cost question has the one-line route answer and a link to the hub FAQ; the options band carries Home's line that program sizes are not a commitment
 * (a first campus program is read beside "1,000–2,500 trainees" otherwise).
 * WP38 (cycle-15 review): the full evidence band (offered-place and attender income, survey chart, education profile) is a light strip, "Evidence from Our Wider Youth Programs": the trial result, the survey's degree share and
 * employment readings, and the two evidence links. The National University band's heading names the partnership, and its clarifying sentence stays under it.
 * WP39 (cycle-16 review): "What Your Students Get" is three short cards (IncludesBand), not the concern / inclusion / benefit matrix; the Guide band no longer repeats the National University partnership sentence
 * ("The National University Partnership" states it).
 * WP43 (cycle-20 review): the light evidence strip WP38 made ("Evidence from Our Wider Youth Programs": the trial line, the survey line and two links) is gone, because the first band already ends in the linked strip
 * "Broader Evidence from Our Youth Programs" (the trial, the survey, the case studies) and the later strip said it again; the page has no #proof-band now (no page linked it). The survey's degree share stayed in the meta description until WP54.
 * WP47 (owner decision 2026-10-15): the page opens with its own proof and goes straight to its offer. The Cost of Waiting band ("No Placement Evidence Weakens Your Employment Story") and the Imagine band ("What Your Students
 * Leave With") are gone; Home carries them. Nothing on this page depended on them: the certification terms (eligibility, attempts and terms agreed in the program scope), the campus labs as
 * blended-learning centers and the follow-up surveys are stated in the delivery model and in "What Your Students Get". The "Degree Holders Struggle to Find Work" card says "A degree alone does not guarantee a job offer."
 * WP49 (cycle-24 reviews): the institution's pain says what it needs ("Your institution needs placement data it can report to a board or ministry."); "Choose Where to Start" no longer repeats the cost answer's pricing sentence in its lead (the
 * "What Does It Cost?" answer states it; the lead is the program-sizes note); the risk band's eyebrow is "Managed Rollout"; the steps band is "What Happens Next".
 * WP50 (cycle-25 review): the track-record band opens with its origin line ("Since 2014, ..."): the empathy line that restated the problem ("You see capable students finish their degrees and still struggle to find work, and you are asked for
 * placement results you cannot yet show.") is gone from it, because the problem band above says it. EMPATHY.universities stays in copy.ts for JobReady@Campus, where the sentence is its problem band's lead.
 * WP51 (cycle-26 review): the institution's pain is headed "Build Placement Results You Can Publish" (it presumed a deficiency); the closing line under "What Happens Next" ("University partners include National University, the University for Peace
 * (UPEACE) and The City College of New York (CCNY).") is gone, because the three universities are already named above it: "The National University Partnership" band lists them in its University Partners tile (PA-05), and the Track Record band's logo strip (#guide) carries them as logo alt text.
 * WP57 (cycle-29 review, Grok R5): "Choose Where to Start" has no size cards. Its recommended card read as a 1,000–2,500 country-pilot size for a campus program; the band is now its heading and one line, "Start with one campus: cohort size, tracks
 * and labs are set in the discovery session.", and the page keeps its own one primary button (hero, call to action and sticky bar). The program-sizes note that qualified the cards (PROGRAM_SIZES_NOTE) is not on this page any more.
 * WP66 (owner request 2026-10-20): the Track Record band has one proof line, the signed-agreement sentence for universities and colleges (SC-11b, `signed` on PartnerGuideBand: "CodersTrust has signed MOUs, agreements or contracts with ... universities and colleges."); the band's heading says "Since 2014", so the sentence leaves the year to it.
 */
import DueDiligenceView from '../../../components/pages/hub/DueDiligenceView.astro';
import LearnerVoice from '../../../components/pages/impact/LearnerVoice.astro';
import LandingLayout from '../../../layouts/LandingLayout.astro';
import HeroBand from '../../../components/sections/HeroBand.astro';
import DefinitionBand from '../../../components/sections/DefinitionBand.astro';
import ProblemBand from '../../../components/sections/ProblemBand.astro';
import MechanismBand from '../../../components/sections/MechanismBand.astro';
import IncludesBand from '../../../components/sections/IncludesBand.astro';
import FAQBand from '../../../components/sections/FAQBand.astro';
import RiskReversalBand from '../../../components/sections/RiskReversalBand.astro';
import CTABand from '../../../components/ui/CTABand.astro';
import PairedEvidence from '../../../components/pages/partners/PairedEvidence.astro';
import GainsPains from '../../../components/pages/partners/GainsPains.astro';
import PartnerGuideBand from '../../../components/pages/partners/PartnerGuideBand.astro';
import RouteLink from '../../../components/pages/partners/RouteLink.astro';
import OfferCards from '../../../components/pages/partners/OfferCards.astro';
import StepsBand from '../../../components/pages/partners/StepsBand.astro';
import Reinforcement from '../../../components/pages/partners/Reinforcement.astro';
import PageEnhancements from '../../../components/pages/partners/PageEnhancements.astro';
import { HOURS, LINKS, TRACKING_MONTHS, meta } from '../../../components/pages/partners/partners';
import { HEADLINE, POSITIONING, READ_THE_EVIDENCE, SPEED_UNIVERSITIES, VALUE_PROPOSITION } from '../../../data/copy';
import { faqJsonLd } from '../../../lib/faq';
import { cta } from '../../../lib/mailto';
import { webPage } from '../../../lib/schema';

const PATH = '/partner-with-us/universities/';
const primary = cta('campus');

// WP54 (cycle-28 review, Kimi K4): the description states only what the page body states (the hero's "universities and colleges" and "Our Approach": "JobReady@Campus combines training, mentoring and placement support in campus labs alongside
// academic studies"). It carried the survey's 84.6% degree share ("Among surveyed completers, 84.6% hold a bachelor’s degree or higher."), a figure that is not on this page.
const { title, description } = meta(
  'JobReady@Campus for Universities and Colleges',
  'For universities and colleges: JobReady@Campus combines training, mentoring and placement support in campus labs, alongside academic studies.',
);

// Q8-route: the one-line cost answer with a link to the partner hub FAQ, which keeps the full answer (WP36).
const FAQ_IDS = ['Q1-campus', 'Q10-campus', 'Q8-route'];
// WP57 (cycle-29 review, Grok R5): the one line that replaces the size cards of "Choose Where to Start".
const START_LINE = 'Start with one campus: cohort size, tracks and labs are set in the discovery session.';
---

<LandingLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  path={PATH}
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Partner with Us', href: LINKS.hub }, { label: 'Universities' }]}
  jsonLd={[webPage({ path: PATH, name: title, description }), faqJsonLd('universities', PATH, FAQ_IDS)]}
  stickyCta={{ label: primary.label, href: primary.href }}
>
  <!-- C1 · Identity hook -->
  <HeroBand
    audience="For Universities and Colleges"
    title={HEADLINE.universities}
    lead={VALUE_PROPOSITION.universities}
    cta={{ label: primary.label, href: primary.href }}
    artSeed="partners-universities"
  />
  <RouteLink kicker="See the Program" label="See Campus Delivery Details" href={LINKS.campus} />
  <!-- GEO · What is CodersTrust? -->
  <DefinitionBand />

  <!-- Compact NU proof band, before the challenge (WP24a) -->
  <PairedEvidence
    eyebrow="Our Partnerships"
    title="The National University Partnership"
    lead="These figures describe National University’s size and the learners being onboarded; they are not learners trained by CodersTrust."
    items={[
      { id: 'SC-04', label: 'Official Training Partner' },
      { id: 'SC-05', label: 'National University' },
      { id: 'PA-05', label: 'University Partners' },
    ]}
  />
  <LearnerVoice story="maria-dewan" excerpt="Maria Dewan was a third-year Biology student when she first came across Her Power, where CodersTrust was a training partner." program="Her Power" tone="white" />

  <!-- C2 · Problem. WP34 (cycle-11 review): the Bangladesh graduate-unemployment tile (PX-03) is gone from this global page; the employer-skills tile (PX-05) stays. -->
  <ProblemBand
    title="Degrees Are Not Turning into Jobs"
    bluf="Capable students finish their degrees, and employers still say they cannot find the skills they need."
    factIds={['PX-05']}
  >
    <GainsPains
      slot="lead"
      pains={[
        // WP46 (cycle-22 review): the employers' pain is the 72% tile directly below (PX-05, worldwide), so a card that restated it is gone; the two pains left are the students' and the institution's.
        { q: 'Degree holders struggle to find work', text: 'A degree alone does not guarantee a job offer.' },
        // WP38 (cycle-15 review): a general institutional pain, stated in one line like its neighbor; it rests on no CodersTrust fact.
        // WP49 (cycle-24 review): the line says what the institution needs ("is rarely collected" was a claim about the whole sector).
        // WP51 (cycle-26 review): the pain is headed as the goal ("Build Placement Results You Can Publish"); it was "Institutions Lack Placement Results They Can Publish", which presumed the reader's institution is deficient. The line under it is unchanged.
        // WP58 (cycle-30 review, GLM L4): the pain is stated as a pain, "Placement Results Are Hard to Publish" (the goal-framed "Build Placement Results You Can Publish" sat inside a list of pains). The line under it is unchanged.
        { q: 'Placement results are hard to publish', text: 'Your institution needs placement data it can report to a board or ministry.' },
      ]}
    />
  </ProblemBand>

  <!-- C3 (Cost of Waiting) and C4 (Imagine) are left to Home since WP47 (owner decision 2026-10-15). -->

  <!-- C5 · Guide. -->
  <!-- WP39 (cycle-16 review): no authority bullet here: "The National University Partnership" (the first band) states the NU relationship, so the Guide band keeps the origin line, the method line and the logos.
       WP50 (cycle-25 review): no empathy line either: the band opens with the origin line, since the problem band above states the problem (JobReady@Campus keeps the sentence as its own problem band's lead).
       WP66 (owner request 2026-10-20): the band's one proof line is the signed-agreement sentence for universities and colleges (SC-11b, `signed`); it is not the National University relationship, which the first band still states once. -->
  <PartnerGuideBand
    signed="SC-11b"
    method={{ text: 'JobReady@Campus runs training in parallel with academic studies, and TalentLEAP organizes skills into career paths.', link: { label: 'How TalentLEAP Works', href: LINKS.talentleap } }}
    partnerGroup="academic"
  />

  <!-- C6 · Mechanism (JobReady@Campus) -->
  <MechanismBand
    title="JobReady@Campus: Training Alongside the Degree"
    positioning={POSITIONING.universities}
    blocks={[
      { label: 'Set Up', title: 'Campus Labs as Learning Centers', text: 'On-campus labs become blended-learning centers with certified local facilitators; faculty members act as coordinators.', icon: 'landmark' },
      { label: 'Prepare for Certification', title: 'Industry Certification Tracks', text: `${HOURS} training hours per certification, with exam preparation; eligibility, attempts and terms are agreed in the program scope.`, icon: 'award' },
      { label: 'Mentor and Place', title: 'Mentoring and Placement', text: `Three months of milestone-based mentoring and placement support, with outcome tracking for ${TRACKING_MONTHS} months after each course, as agreed in the program scope.`, icon: 'users' },
      { label: 'Alongside Studies', title: 'In Parallel with the Degree', text: 'Training runs in parallel with academic studies, with professional internships where employer placements are available.', icon: 'graduation-cap' },
    ]}
    link={{ label: 'About JobReady@Campus', href: LINKS.campus }}
  />

  <!-- C7 · Proof: the National University partnership band opens the page, before the challenge, and ends in the linked strip "Broader Evidence from Our Youth Programs" (the trial, the survey, the case studies). WP43 (cycle-20 review): the second
       evidence band that stood here ("Evidence from Our Wider Youth Programs": the trial line, the survey line and two of the same links) is gone; it said again what that strip links, and no page linked its anchor (#proof-band). -->

  <!-- C8 · Features to benefits. WP39 (cycle-16 review): three short cards in place of the concern / inclusion / benefit matrix, in the order of the three pains in C2 (degree holders struggle to find work; employers cannot find the
       skills they need; build placement results you can publish). Each sentence rests on the register: PD-02 and PD-01 (certification exam preparation, three months of milestone-based mentoring), PD-10 and PD-02
       (tracks set from employer demand, an AI-ready curriculum), PD-08 and PD-09 (follow-up surveys, monthly reports, documentary evidence where available). -->
  <IncludesBand
    title="What Your Students Get"
    cards={[
      { icon: 'award', title: 'Certification Exam Preparation and Mentoring', text: 'Industry certification exam preparation by track, followed by three months of milestone-based mentoring toward a first client or a first job.', facts: ['PD-02', 'PD-01'] },
      { icon: 'briefcase', title: 'Skills Employers Ask For', text: 'Tracks are set from employer demand in an AI-ready curriculum, built around the skills employers say they cannot find.', facts: ['PD-10', 'PD-02'] },
      { icon: 'clipboard-check', title: 'Placement Results You Can Discuss', text: 'Follow-up surveys, monthly reports and documentary evidence where available, as agreed in the program scope, give your institution outcome data it can report.', facts: ['PD-08', 'PD-09'] },
    ]}
  />

  <!-- C9 · Objections -->
  <FAQBand
    audience="universities"
    ids={FAQ_IDS}
    title="Questions Universities Ask"
  />

  <!-- C10 · Differentiation: the positioning statement opens C6; the comparison table is on Home and Investors only (WP30c). -->

  <!-- C11 · Offer. WP57 (cycle-29 review, Grok R5): no size cards, so no pilot size is recommended to a campus; the band is its heading and one line (OfferCards with no cards), and it holds no button of its own. -->
  <OfferCards eyebrow="" title="Choose Where to Start" lead={START_LINE} cards={[]} />

  <!-- C12 · Risk reversal (immediately before C13). WP34 (cycle-11 review): the four diligence cards repeated what this page's bands state, so one item and a link stand in -->
  <DueDiligenceView brief id="due-diligence" />
  <RiskReversalBand
    title="Start with a Pilot, Then Decide on Evidence"
    points={[
      { icon: 'rocket', title: 'A Pilot Comes First', text: 'Start with a first campus program and see its results.' },
      { icon: 'target', title: 'Scorecard Thresholds', text: 'If a threshold is missed, a corrective plan is triggered.' },
      { icon: 'handshake', title: 'Expansion Is Your Decision', text: 'Expansion is your institution’s decision.' },
      { icon: 'shield', title: 'Independent Evaluation Welcome', text: 'We support third-party evaluation of outcomes.' },
    ]}
  />

  <!-- C13 · Call to action -->
  <CTABand
    id="cta"
    heading="Let’s Bring JobReady@Campus to Your Students"
    cta={{ label: primary.label, href: primary.href }}
    secondary={{ label: READ_THE_EVIDENCE, href: LINKS.evidence }}
    urgency={SPEED_UNIVERSITIES.text}
  />

  <!-- C14 · Next steps -->
  <StepsBand
    steps={[
      { title: 'Discovery Session', text: 'A conversation about your students, programs and timeline.' },
      { title: 'Co-Design', text: 'Tracks and campus labs are shaped with you.' },
      { title: 'Agreement', text: 'Scope, schedule and success measures are agreed.' },
      { title: 'First cohort in training', text: 'Certified facilitators begin the first cohort in your labs.' },
    ]}
  />
  <Reinforcement logos={false} reminder={false} />

  <PageEnhancements />
</LandingLayout>
